through read_at. parts/resolve_changes.py:1420 sets `read_at = drawn.unit if source in _COMPUTED else \"\"` (_COMPUTED = compare, levers), and that read_at becomes ChartBlock.unit (parts/charting.py:276) and the table's read_at (blocks.py:1184). The forest always passes drawn.unit (resolve_changes.py:1311), which is why CV2's forest ('Row | Change | 95% interval | Note') and Kairo's change chart are fixed. Failing scenario: a written page plans `diverging_bars` over `source: strata` (or contrasts) on the pass rate. Its row texts are the decided digits (`_decided(..., printed.digits, _end_digits(ends))`, unit-less), `_table_unit('+num:0', '')` returns '', and the Markdown/HTML values table reads `| Overall | +10 | -29 to +58 |` under 'Row | Value | 95% interval', which is the defect residual 5 names and the CHANGELOG entry says is fixed ('A chart's values table writes the unit its values are read in where its format names none'). The new test test_rule_3_on_a_chart_read_in_points_its_values_table_names_the_unit builds a BarsChart and passes read_at='pts' by hand, so it never checks what a resolver passes. Fix by construction: let every change chart's values table read its unit from the drawn Quantity (carry drawn.unit on the block for the table, or pass read_at=drawn.unit for every diverging source, since rows with decided texts are not re-spelled by it). Then add a resolver-level test: resolve a diverging_bars chart of strata and of contrasts in points on Kairo and assert the values-table row ends 'pts'.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/parts/resolve_changes.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report/charts.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_number_policy_every_table.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "blocking", "title": "The report-input change that the builder's claim (1) rests on for CV2's written page has no test: a measure reached only through bundle.readings.measures now carries a unit (`\"unit\": _unit(described, grade)`), and `_unit` also widens to unit-less booleans via reads_as_share. No assertion checks either", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. report_input_build.py:707-716 adds the 'unit' key to the facts of a measure that only a measurement's readings carry. Before this change that path wrote no unit, so the written page's Full results tables ('Every arm by measure', 'Every corrected comparison') printed such a share bare ('0 / 0', '-0.49 to +0.49'), which is CV2's residual 1. report_input_build.py:1061 (`_unit`) now also classes a unit-less boolean that has no grade as 'share', which the old inline rule (value_range == (0, 1) only) did not. Failing scenario: revert the new 'unit' line in the readings loop and every test still passes. test_number_policy_every_table's `_with_measure` adds the fraction to cell_measures, so it reaches measure_facts (already 'share' before this chunk), and `_page_rows` reads the code page, not the written page. test_report_input_build.test_a_measurements_readings_reach_its_measures checks only `.mean`. The hot-path oracle hashes may cover it by accident, but no assertion states it. Add a test that builds a report input from a measurement bundle whose 0-to-1 unit-less measure appears only in readings.measures (shape s3 or a variant of it) and asserts `built.measures[name].unit == 'share'`, plus its written-page Full results row reading '%'. Add one case for a unit-less boolean that is not a check.", "files": ["packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/analysis/report_input_build.py", "packages/evals/src/threetears/evals/kernel/metrics.py", "packages/evals/tests/test_report_input_build.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No recorded test evidence for the reviewed commit, and the chunk knowingly moves rung 5's judge input with the re-record deferred to integration", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `prawduct-hook test-status` reports 'stale: no .test-evidence.json on d